+            <section id="privacy">
+              <header class="major">
+                <h3>Privacy Notice</h3>
+              </header>
+              <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 14, 2026</p>
+              <p>
+                Guam Scholars is an independent educational resource for students, families, and other
+                visitors looking for scholarships, programs, competitions, college information, and related
+                opportunities. I respect your privacy and aim to collect as little information as possible.
+              </p>
+              <h4>Information you choose to send</h4>
+              <p>
+                You can use the contact form at the bottom of the site to suggest an opportunity, report an
+                update, or send a question. When you submit the form, I receive the information you choose to
+                provide, which may include your name, email address, and message. Name is optional. Email is
+                required so I can reply when a response is appropriate.
+              </p>
+              <p>
+                Please do not send sensitive personal information through the form. This includes Social
+                Security numbers, student identification numbers, account passwords, financial information,
+                medical information, application documents, or anything else you would not want sent by
+                ordinary email.
+              </p>
+              <h4>How I use form messages</h4>
+              <p>
+                I use messages only to review suggestions, correct information, consider opportunities for
+                the site, and respond when appropriate. I may not be able to respond personally to every
+                submission. Only I can access the messages I receive through the form. I keep messages only
+                for as long as I decide they are needed to review, respond to, or address the submission, then
+                I delete them.
+              </p>
+              <h4>Service providers and hosting</h4>
+              <p>
+                Guam Scholars is hosted through GitHub Pages. The contact form is processed by FormSubmit.
+                These services may process information needed to host the site or deliver your form message
+                under their own terms and privacy practices. This notice does not control their independent
+                practices. You can review the
+                <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>
+                and
+                <a href="https://formsubmit.co/privacy.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FormSubmit Privacy Policy</a>
+                for more information.
+              </p>
+              <p>
+                I do not operate user accounts, analytics, social-media widgets, or embedded media on Guam
+                Scholars. Guam Scholars does not currently use advertising or advertising trackers. If I add
+                advertising or another service that changes how visitor information is handled, I will update
+                this Privacy Notice before or when that change takes effect.
+              </p>
+              <p>
+                The site contains links to third-party organizations and resources. If you follow one of those
+                links, that organization’s privacy practices apply to its own website.
+              </p>
+              <h4>Corrections and deletion requests</h4>
+              <p>
+                If you want me to correct or delete a message you previously sent through the form, please use
+                the same website form. Include the email address you used and the approximate date of your
+                submission so I can locate it. I will make a reasonable effort to address the request when I
+                can.
+              </p>
+              <h4>Changes to this notice</h4>
+              <p>
+                I may update this notice as Guam Scholars changes. The date at the top of this section shows
+                when it was last updated.
               </p>
